  "assertions": [
    "Null, messageerror and unexpected replies settle pending RPCs and terminate the faulty endpoint instead of retaining CPU leases.",
    "Transport faults never invent an allocator domain or reclaim unrelated stores.",
    "SIFT and elastic tile retries reprepare detached input only for the failed tile and consume completed peers exactly once.",
    "Five comparable failures without useful progress are terminal, preserving the shared guard rather than downgrading the worker ceiling.",
    "Real native SIFT outputs are bitwise identical across the injected message failure and actual ArrayBuffer RangeError; all three worker slots remain admitted.",
    "Explicit native Wasm allocation errors retain their domain; ArrayBuffer errors retain their original evidence. Numerical memory-access-out-of-bounds is not reclassified as allocation refusal.",
    "A local automatic GPU fallback remains available only for explicit GPU unavailability/device loss, with no transport-triggered global provider change.",
    "Native dense 12/128-dimensional, tie, overflow, symmetric, changing grant/cache, GPU staging and cancellation regression assertions pass."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The dense field aborts its current partly-mutated native field on transport failure; the outer field recovery owns any exact fresh-field restart. This patch does not attempt to replay a native propagation fragment.",
    "SIFT output acceptance is not replayed because append/ranking publication lacks an idempotent contract; only safe tile preparation/computation is retried locally.",
    "Injected faults and development watchdogs are test-only. No runtime calibration, warmup, timeout or benchmark was added.",
    "The first browser fault-fixture attempt lost its initial command during a dynamic import. The fixture now queues startup messages; that harness failure was not treated as engine evidence. All final commands reported exit 0."
  ],
  "rawLogs": {
